WEBVTT

00:18.768 --> 00:23.440
So, there's someone else across the world
who got resurrected

00:23.523 --> 00:25.859
and uses science like Senku does!

00:26.985 --> 00:30.905
Well, of course, I'm not that special.

00:30.989 --> 00:34.534
Scientific knowledge
was shared all over the world.

00:34.617 --> 00:36.828
If you enjoy it,
it's just a matter of reading.

00:37.412 --> 00:40.790
Do you mean that they managed
to steadily go from stone axes

00:40.874 --> 00:43.376
to machine guns the way you did, Senku?

00:44.127 --> 00:47.338
That's something more than
just "enjoying" it, don't you think?

00:47.422 --> 00:51.885
It's all just speculation
until we actually make contact.

00:52.385 --> 00:53.845
We only know for certain

00:53.928 --> 00:57.348
that there are scientists
among the resurrected.

00:57.432 --> 00:58.475
That, and…

00:59.059 --> 01:03.730
Yes, their science is
a bit more advanced than ours.

01:07.192 --> 01:09.986
At least regarding armaments.

01:11.988 --> 01:13.615
And most importantly,

01:13.698 --> 01:16.326
they're determined to kill us.

01:24.083 --> 01:26.795
There's an engine coming right behind us!

01:27.462 --> 01:28.379
Are they chasing us?

01:28.463 --> 01:31.549
No way, I've been
keeping watch all this time.

01:32.133 --> 01:34.552
There are no boats
on sight at this moment.

01:34.636 --> 01:37.847
If we keep this speed until tomorrow,
we'll put enough distance between us.

01:37.931 --> 01:40.767
I'm sure they won't be able to catch us.

01:44.187 --> 01:46.731
Wait, what's this sound?

01:51.444 --> 01:53.613
Are you kidding me?

01:53.696 --> 01:54.864
Come on!

02:21.015 --> 02:26.479
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA <i>JUMP COMICS</i>

04:03.868 --> 04:04.911
Senku!

04:04.994 --> 04:07.956
Senku! Senku!

04:09.666 --> 04:11.042
What do we do?

04:11.125 --> 04:12.752
Should we wave "Hi"
and introduce ourselves?

04:12.835 --> 04:15.964
We have no choice but to surrender
for now, don't we?

04:16.047 --> 04:18.633
We could try to talk amicably…

04:19.509 --> 04:22.220
To the ones who shot us
the moment they saw us?

04:25.014 --> 04:25.974
Unfortunately for us,

04:26.057 --> 04:28.768
they wouldn't be flying that low
if they weren't here to attack us!

04:30.687 --> 04:32.563
Hold on tight, folks. We're leaving!

04:33.189 --> 04:34.983
Full speed ahead!

05:11.811 --> 05:13.354
They're coming!

05:38.713 --> 05:42.300
It hurts!

05:42.383 --> 05:45.011
It's just a scratch.
Nothing to worry about.

05:45.094 --> 05:48.306
Matsukaze, cover me! Please, Matsukaze…

05:48.389 --> 05:51.100
Calm down! It's not a serious injury!

05:51.184 --> 05:54.312
You're not actually hurt
to begin with, Ginro.

05:56.064 --> 05:57.565
Go down, go down already!

05:57.648 --> 06:00.735
You're wasting bullets!
There's no way you're going to hit it!

06:00.818 --> 06:03.237
It's the only thing at hand right now.

06:03.321 --> 06:05.281
We can't escape either!

06:17.543 --> 06:18.628
It's in the sun!

06:18.711 --> 06:22.465
They're set on killing us
no matter what, aren't they?

06:37.563 --> 06:41.109
You never know
where something might come in handy.

06:41.859 --> 06:43.027
What's that bottle?

06:43.111 --> 06:46.197
No idea! Can't you ask later?

06:47.657 --> 06:49.283
Kirisame!

06:53.621 --> 06:57.750
I'm counting on your throwing skills.
Tell me what you need!

06:57.834 --> 07:00.378
Solid footing and a rope!

07:05.967 --> 07:07.218
They're coming again!

07:41.335 --> 07:44.547
They took out the engine in a single shot.

07:50.678 --> 07:52.180
I got this.

08:02.190 --> 08:03.566
-We did it!
-We did it!

08:03.649 --> 08:05.109
Hooray!

08:07.236 --> 08:08.738
How did she do it?

08:17.121 --> 08:19.457
<i>That's acetylene gas.</i>

08:19.540 --> 08:21.250
<i>It's harmless to the human body,</i>

08:21.334 --> 08:23.461
<i>but if its concentration</i>
<i>gets above one percent,</i>

08:23.544 --> 08:24.504
<i>the engine shuts down.</i>

08:25.421 --> 08:27.757
What a fancy way to shoot me down.

08:31.052 --> 08:33.638
What's that weapon called again,
Pyro-something?

08:33.721 --> 08:35.890
It looks like they learned how to use it.

08:35.973 --> 08:37.391
<i>It's "pyrophoric."</i>

08:38.476 --> 08:40.186
You forget those things

08:40.269 --> 08:42.772
after being petrified
for some thousand years…

08:42.855 --> 08:47.026
<i>It's easy to make</i>
<i>mixing water with calcium carbide.</i>

08:47.109 --> 08:49.654
<i>Calcium carbide is made</i>
<i>grilling shellfish with charcoal--</i>

08:49.737 --> 08:52.949
Okay, I get it. That's enough.

08:59.830 --> 09:01.582
Our enemies have it good, too.

09:02.750 --> 09:05.294
They've got themselves a sharp scientist…

09:06.379 --> 09:08.214
just like you.

09:13.427 --> 09:16.222
They might come again with backup.

09:16.305 --> 09:18.599
Let's just run away. Quick!

09:19.225 --> 09:20.351
Run away?

09:20.434 --> 09:23.479
What are you talking about?
We're doing the opposite!

09:23.563 --> 09:25.731
What's with that perverted look?

09:26.899 --> 09:30.361
This is how it looks when those two agree.

09:30.444 --> 09:32.697
No good can come out of this.

09:34.490 --> 09:38.119
<i>You guys saw where the plane crashed,</i>
<i>didn't you?</i>

09:38.703 --> 09:40.454
<i>We're going to head there</i>

09:40.538 --> 09:43.374
<i>before they manage to call any backup.</i>

09:58.222 --> 09:59.932
There's no one inside.

10:00.558 --> 10:02.018
They've already fled the scene.

10:02.685 --> 10:06.480
Had they been here, we could have
grilled a lot of info out of them.

10:07.064 --> 10:08.983
So, that counts as lost property
now, right?

10:09.066 --> 10:10.610
Yes, it is.

10:10.693 --> 10:11.611
-What?
-What?

10:13.279 --> 10:14.655
Is that so?

10:21.495 --> 10:24.248
YOU FOUND AN
(OUT OF ORDER) AIRPLANE

10:24.332 --> 10:26.751
The righteous Kingdom of Science

10:26.834 --> 10:29.462
accepts this gift with great honor.

10:30.463 --> 10:34.258
Weakening the enemy's forces
to make them our own is a great strategy.

10:34.342 --> 10:36.385
You're not convincing anyone
with those eyes!

10:36.469 --> 10:38.554
You just wanted the plane
for yourselves, right?

10:40.097 --> 10:44.226
Right, when Senku found the plane,

10:44.810 --> 10:48.731
<i>his heart was speaking up,</i>
<i>it was written all over his face…</i>

10:48.814 --> 10:51.525
<i>He was thrilled!</i>

10:55.488 --> 10:57.114
I won't hide it.

11:04.246 --> 11:07.750
Senku, I just found
something really interesting

11:07.833 --> 11:11.545
on the plane we took from the enemy.

11:13.255 --> 11:14.924
This is great!

11:16.675 --> 11:18.511
These are corn leaves and kernels.

11:19.095 --> 11:20.096
I see.

11:20.596 --> 11:23.432
If the enemy chased us with that plane,

11:23.516 --> 11:25.518
it means there must be

11:25.601 --> 11:28.145
a flat area nearby
that can be used as a runway.

11:29.230 --> 11:32.566
I see! A runway in a cornfield!

11:32.650 --> 11:37.279
Normally, retreating after an ambush
would be the standard response.

11:38.239 --> 11:42.618
At this point, the benefits of chasing
them outweigh the risks we might take.

11:43.202 --> 11:45.704
Chase them? But who…

11:45.788 --> 11:47.456
Isn't it obvious?

11:47.540 --> 11:50.376
We're tailing the enemy
that was on the plane.

11:51.085 --> 11:53.003
If there's a chance we find a cornfield,

11:53.087 --> 11:56.715
we could skip a few years
of land clearing and cultivation.

11:57.216 --> 11:59.301
Let's not forget our objective!

11:59.385 --> 12:03.848
We came all this way
just to look for corn.

12:04.348 --> 12:08.894
No, I mean… Who's going to chase them?

12:14.358 --> 12:18.737
Me, the explorer, Gen, the mentalist,
and the gorill…

12:18.821 --> 12:20.448
Kohaku, the guard with sharp eyesight.

12:20.531 --> 12:22.700
We're the best possible trio to tail them!

12:22.783 --> 12:25.453
If there were too many of us,
the enemy would find us.

12:26.328 --> 12:29.874
I knew it, and still I asked…

12:36.755 --> 12:39.049
Is it really this way?

12:39.133 --> 12:41.510
I am positive, Chrome.

12:43.387 --> 12:44.513
Look.

12:44.597 --> 12:46.515
The enemy's footprints!

12:46.599 --> 12:49.143
That's awesome! That's my Gen!

13:04.366 --> 13:07.369
Did I really have to come?

13:07.453 --> 13:09.622
I'm just a mentalist.

13:09.705 --> 13:11.999
This tailing mission seems really easy…

13:15.544 --> 13:17.963
<i>Wait, something feels off.</i>

13:19.131 --> 13:20.841
<i>Are they luring us in?</i>

13:22.343 --> 13:24.678
<i>They must be quite skilled.</i>

13:26.263 --> 13:28.057
This pisses me off.

13:28.140 --> 13:31.810
Are they really challenging a mentalist?

13:32.520 --> 13:37.525
We gave it our all
in the poker match, for real…

13:38.609 --> 13:41.111
It's the only thing I regret,

13:41.195 --> 13:43.948
even if it's just a bit…

13:45.616 --> 13:50.037
I can't afford to go on a losing streak.

13:51.497 --> 13:55.751
We're not taking a single step further,
Chrome, Kohaku…

13:57.545 --> 14:00.005
You two, follow me from behind.

14:00.631 --> 14:04.051
I'll leave a trail of flowers.

14:05.636 --> 14:06.720
Hey!

14:49.388 --> 14:52.933
Hello! Is anyone there?

15:07.406 --> 15:09.408
Who are you? Where did you come from?

15:09.491 --> 15:11.744
I didn't notice you at all!

15:13.162 --> 15:15.456
You're freaking me out!
Stop with the guns!

15:18.083 --> 15:22.463
Are you body-checking me?
I have no weapons!

15:24.048 --> 15:25.966
You've got no weapons.

15:30.679 --> 15:33.807
You're just setting something up
around here, aren't you?

15:34.308 --> 15:35.851
Who the heck are you?

15:40.356 --> 15:41.231
Ta-da!

15:41.315 --> 15:42.524
A magician?

15:42.608 --> 15:44.485
Exactly.

15:44.568 --> 15:47.279
Well, I could know just by touching you.

15:47.363 --> 15:49.657
It's just that your fingers
are stiffening.

15:50.199 --> 15:52.993
You are not a warrior at all.

15:53.661 --> 15:57.581
<i>Unlike your skilled samurai comrades…</i>

15:59.583 --> 16:03.462
I wanted to crush them by striking first.

16:03.545 --> 16:07.299
Well, there's a good amount of things
I'd like to ask you.

16:09.259 --> 16:10.636
So do you, right?

16:10.719 --> 16:14.431
I'll take you to my leader.

16:45.087 --> 16:45.963
Here it is.

17:04.606 --> 17:07.651
<i>This is our enemy's base?</i>

17:19.204 --> 17:20.581
<i>Just as we thought!</i>

17:21.457 --> 17:25.544
<i>There's a corn farm for real, Senku.</i>

17:29.673 --> 17:31.133
<i>A tractor?</i>

17:35.679 --> 17:37.139
<i>And cows too?</i>

17:37.222 --> 17:40.184
<i>So, they've even started dairy farming…</i>

17:44.188 --> 17:48.358
<i>And that's the runway, isn't it?</i>

17:48.442 --> 17:51.111
<i>This means that the plane from before</i>

17:51.195 --> 17:53.238
<i>might not be the only one they've got.</i>

17:54.156 --> 17:57.159
<i>But he's not going to tell me</i>
<i>anything like that, is he?</i>

18:00.829 --> 18:03.916
That's impressive…

18:03.999 --> 18:05.417
That's not it.

18:18.388 --> 18:21.058
<i>What's this? A factory?</i>

18:27.106 --> 18:30.692
Hey, Xeno. You're here, right?

18:30.776 --> 18:32.111
It's your lucky day.

18:32.194 --> 18:35.405
You're our first customer
in the New World.

18:38.867 --> 18:41.036
<i>Just like Senku…</i>

18:42.162 --> 18:45.791
<i>No, it's not. This is more refined.</i>

18:48.043 --> 18:50.546
<i>They're skilled scientists…</i>

18:52.506 --> 18:53.966
<i>for real.</i>

18:58.762 --> 19:00.180
What the heck?

19:00.264 --> 19:02.808
What are you suddenly doing
with that weird chemical?

19:02.891 --> 19:05.394
Don't be scared, it's only salt water.

19:11.692 --> 19:13.443
Nice to meet you.

19:19.783 --> 19:21.743
I hadn't introduced myself yet.

19:22.828 --> 19:27.499
The man over there with the weird habit
of inhaling poisonous gas…

19:27.583 --> 19:31.253
Shut it. They're just cigarettes.

19:31.336 --> 19:34.923
…is Stanley Snyder. He's a former soldier.

19:35.007 --> 19:37.176
Well, he's still a soldier though.

19:37.759 --> 19:38.927
Our soldier.

19:41.138 --> 19:44.516
I'm Dr. Xeno. Who are you?

19:44.600 --> 19:45.934
Where did you come from?

19:46.018 --> 19:49.521
<i>He's too close… Why's he touching my neck?</i>

19:50.439 --> 19:52.399
My name's Gen Asagiri.

19:52.482 --> 19:55.152
I was a magician in Japan…

19:55.235 --> 19:58.655
"Japan"? Did you hear that, Stan?

19:58.739 --> 20:00.657
That's wonderful.

20:00.741 --> 20:02.659
They've managed to become

20:02.743 --> 20:06.288
the Columbus of this stone world
by coming all the way from the East.

20:11.710 --> 20:14.254
<i>There's no way this could be…</i>

20:15.380 --> 20:19.885
<i>Breathing… Sweating… Heart rate…</i>

20:20.969 --> 20:25.140
<i>Is it a polygraph, a lie detector?</i>

20:30.312 --> 20:34.691
<i>Are they really challenging a mentalist?</i>

20:39.154 --> 20:40.614
The Kingdom of Science

20:41.406 --> 20:43.408
is a hellish business!

20:43.492 --> 20:46.370
The leader of the kingdom
is as harsh as a Spartan…

20:47.120 --> 20:49.581
I was just fleeing from it!

20:52.584 --> 20:54.461
The readings are surprisingly stable.

20:55.295 --> 20:58.090
His smooth speech is actually elegant.

20:58.590 --> 21:01.510
So he's saying the truth?
That's good to hear.

21:02.177 --> 21:03.136
No…

21:03.971 --> 21:06.098
Either he's a terribly honest man,

21:06.181 --> 21:09.351
or a terribly good liar.

21:09.977 --> 21:14.231
But it's fine, I like both options.

21:17.776 --> 21:21.405
<i>I'll sneak in for now, Senku.</i>

21:22.906 --> 21:26.159
<i>Let's take it all,</i>

21:26.243 --> 21:28.495
<i>the entire corn farm</i>

21:28.578 --> 21:32.332
<i>full of that huge amount of Revival Fluid.</i>

21:32.958 --> 21:37.045
So, if we take out that scientist leader,
it'll be over in one hit.

21:37.129 --> 21:38.297
<i>What?</i>

21:39.381 --> 21:42.050
What's the name of that scientist?

21:44.052 --> 21:46.680
<i>This is bad!</i>

21:46.763 --> 21:51.560
<i>To be honest, Senku is weak in battles.</i>

21:52.144 --> 21:53.687
<i>He's the kind of person</i>

21:53.770 --> 21:58.567
<i>who would say something like</i>
<i>"I'll fight in place of the strong ones."</i>

21:59.901 --> 22:03.196
The name of that scientist is…

22:07.909 --> 22:11.413
Taiju! It's Dr.Taiju!

22:11.496 --> 22:15.042
This is tempting!

23:53.181 --> 23:55.851
NEXT EPISODE

23:55.934 --> 23:57.811
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:57.894 --> 23:59.646
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM MAY BE
DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL, SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

23:59.729 --> 24:00.856
Subtitle translation by: Silvia
